## Method and reasoning
First DFS on the original graph and record vertices when they finish. Visit in decreasing finish order on the reversed graph. Among unassigned SCCs, the next component cannot reach another unassigned component in that reversed graph, so one traversal labels exactly one SCC. Use explicit DFS frames to handle chains.

Contract each SCC to one vertex. For an edge A→B between components, the last DFS finish in A comes after the last in B: either DFS from A finishes B first, or B had already finished and could never reach A. Thus the next unassigned maximum-finish component has no edge to another unassigned component in the reversed graph.

## Walk through the sample
Vertices 1 and 2 reach each other. The edge from 2 to 3 only goes forward, so 1 and 3 receive different component IDs. A vertex still shares its own ID even if it has no outgoing edge.

## Complexity
O(n+m+q) time and O(n+m) space.

## Reference implementation
~~~
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int n, m, q;
    cin >> n >> m >> q;
    vector<vector<int>> g(n + 1), rev(n + 1);
    while (m--) {
        int u, v;
        cin >> u >> v;
        g[u].push_back(v);
        rev[v].push_back(u);
    }
    vector<int> order, id(n + 1);
    for (int v = 1; v <= n; ++v)
        if (!id[v]) {
            vector<pair<int, size_t>> st{{v, 0}};
            id[v] = -1;
            while (!st.empty()) {
                auto &[u, i] = st.back();
                if (i == g[u].size()) {
                    order.push_back(u);
                    st.pop_back();
                    continue;
                }
                int w = g[u][i++];
                if (!id[w]) {
                    id[w] = -1;
                    st.emplace_back(w, 0);
                }
            }
        }
    for (auto it = order.rbegin(); it != order.rend(); ++it)
        if (id[*it] < 0) {
            int root = *it;
            vector<int> st{root};
            id[root] = root;
            while (!st.empty()) {
                int v = st.back();
                st.pop_back();
                for (int u : rev[v])
                    if (id[u] < 0) {
                        id[u] = root;
                        st.push_back(u);
                    }
            }
        }
    while (q--) {
        int u, v;
        cin >> u >> v;
        cout << (id[u] == id[v] ? "YES" : "NO") << '\n';
    }
}
